4. MODEL COMPARISON: EY vs WS
================================================================================

The two models show fundamentally different driver rankings:

ENERGY YIELD MODEL (v6)                    WINDSPEED MODEL (v2)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rank  Driver              Multiplier       Rank  Driver              Multiplier
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1     |dz|                1.43×            1     Distance            1.53×
2     |log_speedup|       1.29×            2     Flip × Gradient     1.25×
3     Sample Shortfall    1.25×            3     Speedup Diff Std    1.17×
4     Severity fraction   1.24×            4     Sample Shortfall    1.17×
5     Flip × Gradient     1.23×            5     Concentration       1.16×
6     RIX_avg             1.22×            6     Turning Std         1.15×
7     Distance            1.18×            7     Severity fraction   1.14×
8     Turning Std         1.16×            8     |log_speedup|       1.12×
9     Speedup Diff Std    1.15×            9     |dz|                1.12×
10    Concentration       1.15×            10    RIX_avg             1.12×

KEY INSIGHT:
- EY uncertainty is dominated by HEIGHT DIFFERENCE (|dz| is #1)
  → Power curve amplification: same WS error → different power error at
    different heights

- WS uncertainty is dominated by DISTANCE (#1)
  → Wind field decorrelation: further apart → less similar wind conditions

These are measuring different types of prediction error:
- EY captures total energy across all timestamps (cumulative)
- WS captures mean windspeed error (representative value)

